  "format_version": 2,
  "id": "taylor-green-2d",
  "name": "Taylor–Green vortex · periodic 2D",
  "category": "Analytical transient benchmark",
  "description": "Decaying periodic vortex; unit square, Re=100, mapped 64×64 cells, BDF2/PIMPLE, exact spatial initialization.",
  "capabilities": [
    "Workbench",
    "TwoD",
    "Editable",
    "Periodic",
    "Analytical initialization",
    "BDF2",
    "Unvalidated"
  ],
  "expectations": {
    "closed_domain": true,
    "positive_streamwise_flow": false,
    "curved_boundary": false,
    "non_ideal_mesh_quality": false,
    "notes": "Two-dimensional analytical decaying vortex, not the three-dimensional turbulence problem of Taylor & Green (1937). Periodic 2D formulation: Zhu et al., Performance evaluation of the general characteristics-based off-lattice Boltzmann scheme (2016), section 3.1. https://pure.strath.ac.uk/ws/portalfiles/portal/92250359/Zhu_etal_JCP_2016_Performance_evaluation_of_the_general_characteristics_based_off_lattice_Boltzmann.pdf . Similarity-scaled here to U=1, L=1, nu=0.01 (Re=100). k=2*pi/L; u=-U*cos(kx)*sin(ky)*exp(-2*nu*k²*t), v=U*sin(kx)*cos(ky)*exp(-2*nu*k²*t), p/rho=-U²/4*(cos(2kx)+cos(2ky))*exp(-4*nu*k²*t). Compare velocity L2 error, pressure after removing its constant gauge, and mean kinetic energy U²/4*exp(-4*nu*k²*t). Current conformal cyclic path uses first-order upwind; numerical diffusion is expected. Refine both mesh and time step. No numerical validation has been performed."
  },
